<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's National Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1957</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as People's National Congress Reform, PNC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's National Congress is a political party in Guyana founded in 1957 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forbes-burnham">Forbes Burnham</a> after he split from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-progressive-party-the-gambia">People's Progressive Party</a>. Supported mainly by Afro-Guyanese, it led Guyana to independence in 1966 and ruled until 1992, from 1970 under a socialist co-operative republic, in elections widely seen as rigged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-national-congress.jpg" alt="People's National Congress" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prez001 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:People%27s_National_Congress-Reform_Flag_(Guyana).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
